From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:42:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] audioflinger: exempt ViPER from suspend by uuid

The ViPER exemption in isEffectEligibleForSuspend() compares SL_V4A_RE,
which is ViPER4Android RE's implementation uuid
(90380da3-8536-4744-a6a3-5731970e640f), with desc.type. That effect's
type is EFFECT_UUID_NULL, so the exemption never matches: whenever an
app enables an effect on its own session (an in-app equalizer, MusicFX),
ViPER on the output mix (Global mode) is suspended like any other
effect. Compare desc.uuid instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019koBAc5T4WjFHL6bYvou5m
---
 services/audioflinger/Effects.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/audioflinger/Effects.cpp b/services/audioflinger/Effects.cpp
index 0e0c142e1a..6e67e87671 100644
--- a/services/audioflinger/Effects.cpp
+++ b/services/audioflinger/Effects.cpp
@@ -3018,7 +3018,7 @@ bool EffectChain::isEffectEligibleForSuspend(const effect_descriptor_t& desc)
           (memcmp(&desc.type, SL_IID_DAP, sizeof(effect_uuid_t)) == 0) ||
           (memcmp(&desc.type, SL_IID_DAP_SW, sizeof(effect_uuid_t)) == 0) ||
           (memcmp(&desc.type, SL_IID_DAP_OFFLOAD, sizeof(effect_uuid_t)) == 0) ||
-          (memcmp(&desc.type, SL_V4A_RE, sizeof(effect_uuid_t)) == 0) ||
+          (memcmp(&desc.uuid, SL_V4A_RE, sizeof(effect_uuid_t)) == 0) ||
           (memcmp(&desc.type, SL_AXFX, sizeof(effect_uuid_t)) == 0) ||
           (memcmp(&desc.type, SL_IID_DYNAMICSPROCESSING, sizeof(effect_uuid_t)) == 0)))) {
         return false;
